SPlus Addicts

Here is a very versatile way of transfering S plots to whatever.

David L. Favin

--------------------------------------------------------------------
"clip"<-
function(cmd, width = 7, height = 6, ps = 16)
{
#This program allows one to take plots and place them on the clipboard.
#To run this program
#             clip(Sprogname)
#All lines that place output to screen or printer must be commented out. 
#For example if "win.graph" appears. It has to be changed to "#win.graph".

        win.printer(width, height, format = "metafile", file = 
                "clipboard", scale = "p", pointsize = ps)
        cmd()
        dev.off()
}
----------------------------------------------------------------------
    To transfer a plot from S to PowerPoint and have the capability
    of converting the the plot to PowerPoint objects for editing.
    
    1.Using an S function generate a plot in S. Call this function "s_fun".
    
    2.Run the program called CLIP in the following way:

                    CLIP(s_fun)

      This loads the clip board with the plot.

    3.Open PowerPoint and PASTE the contents of clipboard into PowerPoint.
    
    4.Double click on the plot
    
    5.Select "YES" to Convert the plot to PowerPoint objects.
    
    6.Do the PowerPoint Editing.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
------
    7. You can do the same from EXCEL    

8.Make the graph in EXCEL and copy it to the CLIPBOARD by  ^C  (Control C)

9.Open PowerPoint and using PASTE  SPECIAL chose PICTURE

10. Double clock on the copied picture  and answer YES to the question aout
      making it a PowerPoint object. 

11.Once this is done edit the picture in the usual Power Point way.
