From mcw at ln.nimh.nih.gov  Thu Oct 15 17:34:34 1998
From: mcw at ln.nimh.nih.gov (Matthew Wiener)
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 1998 13:34:34 -0400
Subject: [S] trellis graphics problem resolved: print!
Message-ID: <Pine.SGI.3.96.981015132853.25696C-100000@ln.nimh.nih.gov>

I received lots of replies to my original trellis question.  In brief,
I wanted to know why xyplot wouldn't work inside a function of mine.
The answer is that trellis graphics returns a trellis object, but does not
necessarily print it.  From the command line, printing is automatic, but
from within a function it's not.

Replacing "xyplot(...)" with "print(xyplot(...))" does the trick.

Thanks to:  A. Krause, R. Lancelot, L. Clark, S. Buttrey, D. Bates, B.
Dunlap,  and A. Sinclair.

Matt Wiener

