Dear S-Plusers,

Gratitute to all the friends who proided help generously. 

My first three questions are quite rudimentary and all answers are the same :)

There are different answers to the last two questions. Some replies are as
below:

Solution one:

 rotate vector x by r places
rot.v <- function(x, r) {
    if(r>0) x[c((length(x)-r+1):length(x), 1:(length(x)-r))] else
        x[c((1-r):length(x), 1:-r)]
    }
rot.v(a, 3)
rot.v(a, -2)

Solution 2:

rotate.forward <- function(a, n)
{
    len <- length(a)
    n <- n%%len
    if (n == 0)
        a
    else
        a[c((len-n +1):len, 1:(len -n))]
}

with this function, you just have to type rotate.forward(a, 3)

rotate.backward <- function(a, n){
    len <- length(a)
    rotate.forward(a, len-n)
}

Once again, thank you everybody!

