From rolf at math.unb.ca  Tue Oct 20 13:14:45 1998
From: rolf at math.unb.ca (Rolf Turner)
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 1998 10:14:45 -0300
Subject: [S] Revision to mixreg package.
Message-ID: <199810201314.KAA12835@tanner.math.unb.ca>

It was pointed out to me that the ``mixreg'' package which I posted
on statlib calls upon a function dir.sum() which was not included in
the package.  This function is a ``local enhancement'' that I built
(cribbing from other people on this list) and is automatically
available to me so I never noticed its absence from the package.

I have resubmitted the package with this emendment made, and the
new version, with dir.sum() included is now available.

I would like to take this opportunity to publicly thank the statlib
people for being VERY prompt and helpful with posting the material that
I submitted, almost instantaneously, and for being very patient and
courteous about my multiple revisions of the mixreg package.

                                cheers,

                                        Rolf Turner
