Be warned that "unpaste" is pretty slow, at least on my Splus 4.0 / Windows NT 
setup. It can be quicker to work via "substring", as the following example of 
tab replacement shows:

test> xx_ 'aa\tb;asdf\tasdf;l\t\t;lkjasdf'
test> rep.tabs1_ function( x) paste( unlist( unpaste( xx, '\t')), collapse='  ')
test> rep.tabs1( xx)
[1] "aa  b;asdf  asdf;l    ;lkjasdf"
test> rep.tabs2_ function( x) { yy_ substring( xx, 1:nchar( xx), 1:nchar( xx)); 
yy[ yy=='\t']_ '  '; paste( yy, collapse='') }
test> rep.tabs2( xx)
[1] "aa  b;asdf  asdf;l    ;lkjasdf"
test> dos.time( for( i in 1:1000) rep.tabs1( xx))
[1] 18.50999
test> dos.time( for( i in 1:1000) rep.tabs2( xx))
[1] 4.809998
test> 

Moral: don't do what I did and rewrite your code to avoid "substring" in favour 
of "unpaste"!

